# Commits & PRs (tags required)

Source of truth for allowed types/scopes: `commitlint.config.mjs`. Labels: `docs/delivery/AGILE_PLAN.md` §4.

## Commit message (mandatory)

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary> (<TICKET>)
```

| Part | Rules |
|---|---|
| **type** | `feat` `fix` `perf` `refactor` `test` `docs` `build` `ci` `chore` `revert` `content` `prompt` `adr` |
| **scope** | Exactly one from commitlint `scope-enum` (e.g. `auth`, `rate-limit`, `infra`, `docs`, `repo`) — **never empty** |
| **summary** | Imperative, lowercase start, no trailing `.`, ≤ ~72 chars in the subject; header ≤ 100 |
| **ticket** | `(S<n>-<INITIALS>-<nn>)` at end of subject, e.g. `(S0-VV-04)` |

**Examples**

```text
feat(rate-limit): sliding window lua guard (S1-VV-04)
fix(auth): invalidate refresh token family on reuse (S1-VV-01)
docs(repo): add agent kb and workflow rules (S0-TN-01)
chore(infra): healthchecks for redis and redpanda (S0-VV-01)
```

**Body (optional but preferred for non-trivial changes)**

```text
Why this change exists in 1–3 lines.

- key implementation note
- follow-up / out of scope
```

Refuse vague subjects (`update stuff`, `fix`, `wip`) and commits missing type, scope, or ticket.

## Pull request

### Title

Same shape as the commit subject (Conventional Commit + ticket). Squash-merge uses it.

### Body

Fill `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`:

- **Ticket** id
- **What changed, and why**
- DoD checkboxes

Also include: risk/rollback note if infra/auth/migrations; link related contract PR if any.

### Labels (tags) — apply with `gh pr create --label` / `gh pr edit --add-label`

Every PR must have **at least one priority**, **one area**, and **the sprint** label:

| Kind | Labels |
|---|---|
| Priority | `P0-blocker` · `P1` · `P2-droppable` |
| Area | `area:backend` · `area:frontend` · `area:ai` · `area:data` · `area:infra` · `area:contracts` |
| Sprint | `sprint-0` … `sprint-5` |
| Optional | `needs-contract` · `needs-content` · `blocked` |

**Example**

```bash
gh pr create --base develop \
  --title "feat(rate-limit): sliding window lua guard (S1-VV-04)" \
  --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Ticket
S1-VV-04

## What changed, and why
…

## Definition of Done
- [x] …
EOF
)" \
  --label "P0-blocker" --label "area:backend" --label "sprint-1"
```

Base branch: **`develop`**. Do not open untagged PRs.
